# The backend's direct dependencies, pinned. Edit THIS file, then regenerate the hashed lock
# the production image installs (every transitive dependency, pinned and hashed):
#   pip-compile --generate-hashes --allow-unsafe --strip-extras --no-emit-index-url \
#     --output-file requirements.txt requirements.in      # with Python 3.12, like the image
# CI fails when the two disagree. Dependabot updates both.
# Pinned to the exact versions resolved on python:3.12-slim (the deploy image), so builds
# are reproducible and a compromised/breaking upstream can't slip in on the next build.
# Bump deliberately (watch the CVE notes below). Proper hash-locking (pip-compile) is the
# next step; see docs. Direct deps only — pip resolves transitives.
